        <!-- FAQ -->
        <div class="docs-block reveal-scroll" id="faq">
          <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

          <div class="docs-faq-item">
            <h4>Is ShortDesk really free?</h4>
            <p>Yes. It is 100% free, open-source software released under the MIT License. No hidden fees, no premium tiers.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="docs-faq-item">
            <h4>Do I need an account?</h4>
            <p>No. ShortDesk does not require user accounts. Just paste a URL and shorten it.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="docs-faq-item">
            <h4>Can I use my own domain?</h4>
            <p>Yes, if you self-host. Deploy ShortDesk on your server and configure your domain to point to it.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="docs-faq-item">
            <h4>How long are links stored?</h4>
            <p>Indefinitely, unless you set an expiry date. Self-hosted instances can configure their own retention policies.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="docs-faq-item">
            <h4>Is there an API?</h4>
            <p>Yes. See the <a href="#api">API Reference</a> section above for endpoint details and examples.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="docs-faq-item">
            <h4>How do I report a bug?</h4>
            <p>Open an issue on <a href="https://github.com/aminilay/shortdesk-official/issues" target="_blank">GitHub</a>.</p>
          </div>
